<section class="blk">
  <h2 id="s-household-229">Household 229 &mdash; Sancho's son, and three children nobody had</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>The same sweep turned up a second household: <strong>Pedro Antonio Lerena, son of Sancho</strong>,
    with <strong>Doña Vicenta Vega</strong> &mdash; the wife this archive already holds &mdash; and
    three children it did not.</p>
    <p><strong>His age dates the page.</strong> Born 31 July 1793 and entered at forty, this census is
    about <strong>1833</strong>, not 1858. That is the check that makes the whole reading hold: the
    couple's one previously known child, <strong>Leonarda Margarita, was born in 1837</strong> and is
    correctly absent. Three elder children in 1833, a fourth four years later.</p>
  </div>
