<section class="blk">
  <h2 id="s-maria-casa2">María Llerena, sixty, Spanish, head of her own house</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>The last of the three Llerenas in the census collection, and the one worth the most. She is
    <strong>the first name on her page</strong> &mdash; <strong>&ldquo;Casa 2. María Llerena &mdash; 60
    años &mdash; Española&rdquo;</strong> &mdash; heading her own household, with <strong>Manuel, 20,
    &ldquo;Africana&rdquo;</strong> and <strong>Rosa, 12, &ldquo;Oriental&rdquo;</strong> under her.</p>
    <p><strong>Sancho was <em>andaluz</em> and forty-five in 1812.</strong> Depending on this census's
    date, a Spanish-born Llerena woman of sixty stands in his generation or the one above it &mdash;
    which is exactly the generation this archive cannot get past. <strong>She is attached to him by
    nothing</strong>, and the census year is <strong>not established</strong>, so her sixty cannot yet
    be turned into a birth year. That date, at the top of her own page, is the next step.</p>
  </div>
