<section class="blk">
  <h2 id="s-film-map">The reel, mapped by brightness</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Everything above came off <strong>six images of a reel of three thousand two hundred</strong>.
    The reel is the Archivo General de la Nación's <em>Padrones de Montevideo y Extramuros</em>, and
    until today nobody here knew where one volume ended and the next began.</p>
    <p>It is mapped now, and not by looking. Each thumbnail was drawn to a small canvas and its mean
    brightness measured: <strong>filming target boards read 16&ndash;30, ordinary pages 140&ndash;156</strong>,
    with nothing in between. <strong>Eighteen dark-frame clusters, 1,604 thumbnails, three calls, no session and no screenshots</strong> &mdash; and then every one of them checked. The reel holds <strong>fifteen volumes</strong>, each opening with a title board and closing with a <em>fin del ítem</em> card. Twelve further dark frames turned out to be <strong>book covers, spines and blanks</strong>, which is why a dark frame could not simply be called a boundary.</p>
  </div>
